-----------------------------------------------------
Data sources surfaced via MCP servers or canned data
-----------------------------------------------------

Each MCP server's README documents its specific upstream(s); the
following is the consolidated list. Use of the live APIs is subject
to each agency's terms of service.

  * VectorSurv (https://vectorsurv.org/) — national mosquito + tick
    surveillance API. A snapshot of the v1.0.44 OpenAPI spec is
    redistributed under mcp/vectorsurv/openapi/ for diff-based drift
    detection. Use of the live API requires Gateway credentials and
    is subject to VectorSurv's terms.

  * National Weather Service public API (api.weather.gov) and the
    WPC HeatRisk gridded product (wpc.ncep.noaa.gov/heatrisk/) —
    public-domain works of the U.S. federal government. Polite
    User-Agent required.

  * USGS WHISPers (https://whispers.usgs.gov/) — wildlife mortality
    events. Public-domain U.S. federal data; canned fallback events
    in mcp/whispers-mcp/src/whispers_mcp/canned.py are
    historically-grounded synthetic stand-ins (the canned IDs do not
    resolve to real WHISPers events — by design — see the file
    docstring).

  * iNaturalist public API (https://api.inaturalist.org/v1/) —
    observations are licensed by their individual contributors;
    aggregate use is governed by iNaturalist's terms.

  * MAG Heat Relief Network ArcGIS Feature Service
    (https://geo.azmag.gov/arcgis/rest/services/maps/Heat_Relief_Network/)
    — published by the Maricopa Association of Governments for
    Phoenix-metro cooling-center directory. Canned dataset in
    mcp/mag-hrn-mcp ships 12 representative sites; live mode is
    env-overridable.

  * ADHS public reports — heat-mortality annual summaries, arbovirus
    weekly summaries, reportable-conditions definitions. Canned
    values in mcp/adhs-mcp/src/adhs_mcp/canned_data.py are sourced
    from ADHS-published PDFs and ArcGIS Experience dashboards, cited
    inline in the file docstring (see heat/04-vulnerable-populations.md
    and schema/heat.sql for the upstream citations).

  * 211 Arizona (https://211arizona.org/) — public heat-relief
    directory. Mock data in mcp/211-az-mcp/src/az211_mcp/mock_data.py
    cites the public 211 site in its module docstring; production
    integration requires a partnership agreement with Solari Crisis
    & Human Services.

  * Great Arizona Tick Check (UA Cooperative Extension, Walker Lab,
    UA Tucson Entomology) — no public REST API today. Mock backend
    in mcp/great-az-tick-check-mcp/ ships with explicit attribution
    to the program. Production wiring requires a partnership with
    the Walker Lab.


--------------------
Canned reference data
--------------------

The canned datasets in the MCP servers are documented and cited
inline in the relevant Python files:

  * mcp/adhs-mcp/src/adhs_mcp/canned_data.py — cites
    heat/04-vulnerable-populations.md, schema/heat.sql,
    schema/deep/standards.sql, wildlife/resources.md, and the ADHS
    Vector-Borne & Zoonotic Diseases program page.

  * mcp/whispers-mcp/src/whispers_mcp/canned.py — names the 1993
    Four Corners hantavirus outbreak, 2022+ HPAI H5N1 detections,
    and 2025 plague activity as the historical events the synthetic
    stand-ins are modelled on, with explicit "do not present as
    authoritative" warnings.

  * mcp/211-az-mcp/src/az211_mcp/mock_data.py — cites
    211arizona.org/crisis/heat-relief/ as the live source of truth
    that the mock backend approximates.

  * mcp/inaturalist-mcp/src/inaturalist_mcp/canned_data.py — cites
    the iNaturalist taxa pages and AZ place_id 53 as the authoritative
    references; every taxon ID is env-overridable.

  * mcp/wearable-mcp/src/wearable_mcp/mock_data.py — names the
    HealthKit / Health Connect data shapes the mock profiles mirror,
    with the LOINC metric catalog cited from schema/deep/followups.sql.

  * schema/deep/outbreaks.sql — every historical AZ outbreak row
    carries inline citations to the ADHS, CDC MMWR, USGS WHISPers,
    or peer-reviewed source it draws milestone dates from. Spot-check
    on review: 1993 Four Corners, 2003 AZ WNV emergence, 2014 Yuma
    dengue, 2021 Maricopa WNV, 2023 + 2024 Maricopa heat, 2025
    Coconino plague.


